The year is 3017. The world is changed. Magistrates rule now and they have strict rules.
Every baby born mist have its soul taken and stored in liquid form.
The children will learn to read, write and any necessary skills to help in society.
At the age of 18 a job will be appointed to them according their best skillset in school.
As these, gorwn ups now, complete tasks in their field a little bit of their soul is given back to them before the final judgment of God for Eternal Life or not.
Here we meet Aen. He's 18 years old and the job of cleric has been assigned to him.
A cleric is a potential Magistrate which means his role is seriously important. He's also a good candidate for Eternal Life.
He has to attend to the needs of the people, come up with new tech and most of all, help other magistrates in their decisions and, most important of all, keep secrets. Many secrets.
As he progresses through the cleric ranks, by doing exceptional work, he reaches the rank of Archbishop. Then his first initiation for the rank of Magistrate happens.
Aen takes the initiation right but suddenly a large explosion is heard from outside. Every Magistrate runs outside the room to see what's happening. 
With half his soul recovered Aen sees the Holy Bible on the table and curiosity takes the better of him.
He opens it and goes straight to the end. There he reads:
"Every life, every soul ever conceived is preordained by Us, the Archmagistrates. We define what the world and life is."
Shocked his leaves the Bible back at its place.
He knows he has to keep it a secret but he starts having doubts about this whole society he lives in.
He needs answers and he's stubborn enough to find them.
